<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/classification-assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/02-core-concepts.md#cross-cutting> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/classification-assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Classification Assignment" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/classification-assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A contextual assertion that a resource (e.g. an Award or Population) is classified by a concept from a specified external or internal classification scheme, such as Candid's Philanthropy Classification System. External taxonomies classify CommonGood resources; they do not define those resources -- Need, Population, and Organization remain the ontology's own entities regardless of which taxonomy terms are assigned to them." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/classification-assignment> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/category> "cross-cutting" .
