<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/02-core-concepts.md#organizational-entities> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/role> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Role" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/role> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A contextual capacity an agent occupies, distinct from the agent's permanent identity or classification." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/role> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/category> "organizational-entities" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-active-role-requires-effective-from> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/BusinessRule> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-active-role-requires-effective-from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Role occupancy with status Active must specify Effective From -- a role cannot be considered in effect without a defined start." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-active-role-requires-effective-from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/02-core-concepts.md#organizational-entities> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-active-role-requires-effective-from> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An active role must have an effective start date" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-active-role-requires-effective-from> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/organization-role> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-active-role-requires-effective-from> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/person-role> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-active-role-requires-effective-from> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/role> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/BusinessRule> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An Amendment changes the Grant Agreement going forward; it does not retroactively alter Payments or Reports already completed under the prior terms." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/03-relationships.md#key-relationship-rules-draft> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An Amendment is forward-looking, not retroactive" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/amendment> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/grant-agreement> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/payment> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-amendment-not-retroactive> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/report> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-award-requires-approved-decision> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/BusinessRule> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-award-requires-approved-decision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An Award cannot exist without a Decision that approved an Application (or, in funder-initiated giving, an equivalent internal approval)." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-award-requires-approved-decision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/03-relationships.md#key-relationship-rules-draft> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-award-requires-approved-decision> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An Award requires an approved Decision" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-award-requires-approved-decision> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/application> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-award-requires-approved-decision> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/award> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-award-requires-approved-decision> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/decision> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-allocation-should-sum-to-100> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/BusinessRule> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-allocation-should-sum-to-100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When a classified resource's Classification Assignments for a given scheme carry an Allocation Percentage, those percentages should sum to 100 once the allocation is asserted as complete. An incomplete sum is a data-quality signal to surface, not a gap to silently renormalize or complete on the resource's behalf." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-allocation-should-sum-to-100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/03-relationships.md#classification> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-allocation-should-sum-to-100> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allocation percentages should sum to 100 when allocation is asserted complete" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-allocation-should-sum-to-100> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/award> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-allocation-should-sum-to-100> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/classification-assignment> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-allocation-should-sum-to-100> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/population> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-at-most-one-primary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/BusinessRule> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-at-most-one-primary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "For a given classified resource (e.g. an Award or a Population) and a given classification scheme, at most one Classification Assignment should have Is Primary set to true -- multiple simultaneous primaries make Primary-mode reporting ambiguous about which classification the resource is chiefly attributed to." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-at-most-one-primary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/03-relationships.md#classification> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-at-most-one-primary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "At most one primary Classification Assignment per resource and scheme" .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-at-most-one-primary> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/award> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-at-most-one-primary> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/classification-assignment> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-assignment-at-most-one-primary> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/appliesTo> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/population> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-rolls-up-not-down> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/BusinessRule> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-rolls-up-not-down> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Classification Assignment's Classification Concept Code rolls upward through that concept's Broader chain for reporting purposes -- a resource explicitly classified under a narrower term is implicitly also covered by every broader ancestor. The reverse never holds: a resource explicitly classified under a broader term is not implicitly classified under any of its more specific descendants, since the source data made no claim that specific." .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-rolls-up-not-down> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://github.com/EGovender/commongood-atlas/blob/main/docs/03-relationships.md#classification> .
<https://egovender.github.io/commongood-atlas/ontology/rules/rule-classification-rolls-up-not-down> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Classification rolls upward through broader terms, never downward" .
